<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' maiden 10-year bond coupon at 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippines' maiden 10-year bond coupon at 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' maiden fixed-rate, ten-year bonds fetched a coupon rate of 16.0 percent, the Bureau of Treasury reported on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The auction drew 9.915 billion pesos worth of tenders, resulting in the full award of the two billion-peso offering, the government said.</p>
<p>The lowest rate accepted by the government was 15.50 percent, with the average of the bids awarded at 15.929 percent.</p>
<p>Settlement of the ten-year bonds will be on Thursday.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
